### Problem

We have **7 nearly-identical `DummyCaller` contracts** scattered across different deployment scripts. Each one does the same thing: stores an OPCM address in storage slot 0, then delegatecalls to it with encoded calldata. The only difference is the function signature.

**Current implementations:**

| File | Contract | Function |
|------|----------|----------|
| [`UpgradeOPChain.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/UpgradeOPChain.s.sol#L129-L149) | `DummyCallerV1` | `upgrade(OPContractsManager.OpChainConfig[])` |
| [`UpgradeOPChain.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/UpgradeOPChain.s.sol#L129-L137) | `DummyCallerV2` | `upgrade(OPContractsManagerV2.UpgradeInput)` |
| [`UpgradeSuperchainConfig.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/UpgradeSuperchainConfig.s.sol#L86-L94) | `DummyCaller` | `upgradeSuperchainConfig(ISuperchainConfig)` |
| [`UpgradeSuperchainConfig.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/UpgradeSuperchainConfig.s.sol#L99-L110) | `DummyCallerV2` | `upgradeSuperchain(SuperchainUpgradeInput)` |
| [`AddGameType.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/AddGameType.s.sol#L106-L117) | `DummyCaller` | `addGameType(AddGameInput[])` |
| [`InteropMigration.s.sol`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/packages/contracts-bedrock/scripts/deploy/InteropMigration.s.sol#L229-L240) | `DummyCaller` | `migrate(MigrateInput)` |

All of these follow the exact same pattern:
```solidity
contract DummyCaller {
    address internal _opcmAddr;

    function someFunction(SomeType memory input) external returns (bool, bytes memory) {
        bytes memory data = abi.encodeCall(SomeInterface.someFunction, (input));
        (bool success, bytes memory result) = _opcmAddr.delegatecall(data);
        return (success, result);
    }
}
```

### Solution

Replace all of these with a single generic implementation that uses a `fallback()` function to forward any call:

```solidity
/// @title DummyCallerGeneric
/// @notice Generic delegatecall forwarder. Reads target from storage slot 0,
/// forwards calldata via delegatecall, reverts on failure, returns on success.
contract DummyCallerGeneric {
    address internal _opcmAddr;

    fallback() external {
        address target = _opcmAddr;
        assembly {
            calldatacopy(0, 0, calldatasize())
            let result := delegatecall(gas(), target, 0, calldatasize(), 0, 0)
            returndatacopy(0, 0, returndatasize())
            switch result
            case 0 { revert(0, returndatasize()) }
            default { return(0, returndatasize()) }
        }
    }
}
```

### Tasks

1. Move `DummyCallerGeneric` to a shared location (e.g., `scripts/libraries/DummyCaller.sol`)
2. Update all scripts to use `DummyCaller` instead of their custom implementations
3. Remove the redundant `DummyCallerV1`, `DummyCallerV2`, and `DummyCaller` contracts
4. Update any Go code that references specific DummyCaller artifacts to use the generic one
